> notb(a: bool) = !a
> andb(a: bool, b: bool) = a & b
> orb(a: bool, b: bool) = a | b
> nandb(a: bool, b: bool) = ~(a & b)
> notnand(a: bool) = ~(a & a)
> andnand(a: bool, b: bool) = ~(~(a & b) & ~(a & b))
> equiv notb ~ notnand
notb and notnand are equal on the domain of notb (exhaustive)
> equiv andb ~ andnand
andb and andnand are equal on the domain of andb (exhaustive)
> gates notb basis nand
gates for notb: 1 input bit -> 1 output bit, basis nand
  exact search stopped (cost limit at cost 12); Shannon decomposition instead:
  no program found for output 0 (basis not complete, or more than 244 steps)
> gates andb basis nand
gates for andb: 2 input bits -> 1 output bit, basis nand
  exact search stopped (cost limit at cost 12); Shannon decomposition instead:
  no program found for output 0 (basis not complete, or more than 244 steps)
> gates orb basis nand
gates for orb: 2 input bits -> 1 output bit, basis nand
  minimal: cost 4, 4 steps (no program of cost <= 3 exists; 30 candidates searched)
  checked: the program reproduces every output bit on all 4 care inputs
  t0 = nand(a, b)              = ~(a & b)
  t1 = nand(a, t0)              = ~(a & t0)
  t2 = nand(b, t1)              = ~(b & t1)
  t3 = nand(t1, t2)              = ~(t1 & t2)
  r0 = t3
> gates nandb basis nand
gates for nandb: 2 input bits -> 1 output bit, basis nand
  minimal: cost 1, 1 step (no program of cost <= 0 exists; 1 candidates searched)
  checked: the program reproduces every output bit on all 4 care inputs
  t0 = nand(a, b)              = ~(a & b)
  r0 = t0
